1.Using Cisco Packet Tracer, create a topology and simulate sending a 
simple PDU from source to destination using hub and switch as connecting 
devices and demonstrate ping.
Theory
Cisco Packet Tracer is a network simulation and visualization tool developed by Cisco. It 
allows users to create, configure, and test computer networks without using physical 
networking devices.
In this experiment, a network topology is created using PCs, a hub, and a switch. A Simple 
PDU is used to simulate communication between a source and destination device. The ping
command is used to verify connectivity between the devices.
A Hub operates at the Physical Layer (Layer 1) and broadcasts the received data to all 
connected devices.
A Switch operates mainly at the Data Link Layer (Layer 2) and forwards frames to the 
appropriate destination using MAC addresses.
Ping uses the ICMP (Internet Control Message Protocol) to test whether two network 
devices can reach each other.
Simple PDU in Packet Tracer provides a simple way to test packet delivery between network 
devices and observe whether the communication is successful.
We can create different network topologies using Cisco Packet Tracer. Let us explore 
different network diagrams starting with simple to bit complex.
